  "measurement_notes": [
    "All five run exit codes are external process outcomes: 101, 0, 0, 0, 0. A JSONL terminal summary is emitted before teardown and cannot itself establish native process success.",
    "The failed run completed 30.014 seconds of measurement, then its child aborted with 0xc0000409 after accesskit_windows ClientToScreen returned HRESULT 0x80070578 for an invalid HWND. The outer test process failed with 101.",
    "Final teardown stops the real actor, withdraws active scene/input, blurs for two actual draw opportunities, removes the native window, waits for original HWND destruction, drops retained owners, and quits normally. It does not disable UIA or suppress process failure.",
    "Both publication modes use the same new Release binary, frozen guest package, retained production renderer cache, seed, input cycle, and observer. This compares full viewport publications with patches; it is not a comparison against an old uncached renderer binary.",
    "Warmup cache bases, playhead, and overscan buffer differ between separate starts and are retained in raw headers and analysis. Header comparison covers selected control conditions, not bit-identical warmed state.",
    "prepare/reuse/shape/raster are cumulative work counters. RSS/private/current cache residency/live resources are gauges. Do not infer a memory leak from increasing cumulative work.",
    "observation_ring_evictions records runtime observability Snapshot.dropped: omitted/evicted detailed runtime records, not GPUI profiler rotation. Do not assume every omitted record was read before eviction. Publication completeness is independently checked using Actor calls and consumed Publication records.",
    "fixture_ingress is an Actor-lifetime high-water mark for the fixture adapter with capacity 128, not instantaneous occupancy or production WorkSender queue depth.",
    "Peaks are maxima of one-second observations, not absolute OS peaks. Native GPU atlas memory is unmeasured. This timeline uses zero resident derived-image textures; other retained-cache/native layer evidence covers image resource paths.",
    "Input-to-frame HDR measures native window dispatch to draw, excluding hardware/SendInput dispatch delay; cumulative HDR quantiles must not be averaged or subtracted.",
    "Exact 30-second/steady-phase cumulative counter boundaries are labelled linear interpolation estimates from observed brackets. Actual endpoint deltas and raw timing distributions are preserved separately in analysis."
  ],
